  <data name="TextBox3.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usually a condition is formed using a relational operator
A relational operator determines if a specific relationship exists between two values
	&gt;		Greater than
 	&lt;		Less than
 	=		Equal to
 	&lt;&gt;	          Not equal to
 	&gt;=	          Greater than or equal to
 	&lt;=	          Less than or equal to
</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextBox1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Relational operators are binary – meaning they use two operands, for example:

		length &gt; width	Is length greater than width?
		size &lt;= 10		Is size less than or equal 10?

Relational operators are used in Boolean expressions which yield a True or False result
IF GRD &gt;65.4 OR GRD &lt; 69.5 then GRD = 2.75
</value>
  </data>
